stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> R: fork
    R --> S: waits for something<br/>(signal can wake it)
    S --> R: it arrived
    R --> D: waits on I/O<br/>(signals NOT delivered)
    D --> R: I/O completed
    R --> T: SIGSTOP
    T --> R: SIGCONT
    R --> Z: exit()
    Z --> [*]: parent calls wait()<br/>= reaped

    note right of D
        kill -9 does nothing here.
        The signal is queued until
        the I/O finishes.
    end note

    note right of Z
        Already dead. Holds a PID
        and an exit code, nothing else.
        Signal the PARENT.
    end note
